<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reichsdeputationshauptschluss</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1803">1803</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Imperial Recess of 1803</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Reichsdeputationshauptschluss, or Imperial Recess, was the final resolution of an imperial deputation adopted at Regensburg in 1803. To compensate German princes for lands lost to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> on the left bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, it secularised almost all church states and abolished most imperial cities, handing their territories to the larger princes. It created new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a>, among them Württemberg and Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassel">Kassel</a>, and reshaped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> before the Empire ended in 1806.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reichsdeputationshauptschluss.jpg" alt="Reichsdeputationshauptschluss" width="320" height="370" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original uploader was Känsterle at nl.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Titelseite_des_Reichsdeputationshauptschlusses_vom_25._Februar_1803.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
